<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cannstatter Wasen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1818</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Cannstatter Volksfest</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cannstatter Wasen, or Cannstatter Volksfest, is a large autumn festival held on the Wasen meadows beside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a> at Bad Cannstatt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-wurttemberg">William I of Württemberg</a> founded it in 1818 as an agricultural fair after the famine of 1816–1817, crowned by a tall column decorated with fruit. It has grown into one of the largest beer festivals in the world, second only to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oktoberfest">Oktoberfest</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cannstatter-wasen.jpg" alt="Cannstatter Wasen" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Enslin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cannstatter_Wasen-leer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
